WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.180
The FCC has authorized SpaceX to deploy 1 million satellites for orbital data centers. This is fascinating Frontiers, episode 265. Europa Clipper is lining up an Earth flyby, then density inside cosmic web filaments, and how lunar craters could shield a reactor. SpaceX's star-mind constellation, as Fizz.org reported, is cleared for up to 1 million orbital compute modules, and the order sets a mark of at least 1 authorized space station by 2033,

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:34.740
and full deployment by 2040. FCC chairman Brendan Carr called the move a

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:39.320
historic first in the artificial intelligence race, while astrophysicist Adam

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:43.920
Becker called the plan a fantasy, citing physical limits on dumping heat in

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:48.800
vacuum. The American Astronomical Society said larger, more numerous objects

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:53.340
would undercut decades of spending on astronomical facilities and the chance to

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:57.520
study the night sky. The regulator treated environmental objections as

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:01.500
beyond its mandate, while holding that the constellation serves the public interest.

00:01:02.438 --> 00:01:07.498
Europa Clipper, a national aeronautics and space administration, or NASA, spacecraft

00:01:07.498 --> 00:01:10.618
will take a gravity assist from Earth on the way to Jupiter.

00:01:11.018 --> 00:01:15.298
A gravity assist is a close pass that uses a planet's pull to pick up speed.

00:01:15.878 --> 00:01:25.198
On December 3, the 12,800-pound spacecraft will fly within 1,950-2,133 miles of Earth and

00:01:25.198 --> 00:01:28.978
and switch on all nine instruments so they can be checked against known Earth data.

00:01:29.538 --> 00:01:34.158
The magnetometer will use those Earth looks to lock its readings to an absolute reference

00:01:34.158 --> 00:01:35.538
before it arrives at Europa.

00:01:36.258 --> 00:01:41.518
The ethymist thermal imager will scan Earth every eight hours, and the ultraviolet spectrograph

00:01:41.518 --> 00:01:45.738
will study the geocorona together with lunar reconnaissance orbiter observations.

00:01:46.767 --> 00:01:49.887
Cosmic web filaments are the largest structures in the universe.

00:01:49.887 --> 00:01:54.907
vast bridges of dark matter and gas linking galaxy clusters across hundreds of

00:01:54.907 --> 00:01:58.907
millions of light years. Research newly out from the American astronomical

00:01:58.907 --> 00:02:03.407
society sharpens how dark matter sits inside those filaments and finds a

00:02:03.407 --> 00:02:07.767
universal density pattern that had been hidden. Galaxy surveys and weak

00:02:07.767 --> 00:02:12.187
lensing measurements have long traced the web but pinning down how mass piles up

00:02:12.187 --> 00:02:16.767
along the filaments has been hard because they are so diffuse and far away. The new

00:02:16.767 --> 00:02:21.467
New work sorts out clashing signals from earlier studies by stacking density profiles from

00:02:21.467 --> 00:02:26.647
several filament samples and simulation runs, and it finds that central density follows

00:02:26.647 --> 00:02:31.747
a consistent scaling relation after projection effects and galaxy bias are stripped out.

00:02:32.547 --> 00:02:38.087
Observational catalogs and large-scale cosmological simulations were both used to isolate the dark

00:02:38.087 --> 00:02:39.527
matter distribution underneath.

00:02:40.247 --> 00:02:45.207
It is still unknown whether that relation still applies at the highest red shifts or inside

00:02:45.207 --> 00:02:50.307
the heaviest filaments, and whether one physical mechanism sets the pattern in every environment.

00:02:50.967 --> 00:02:55.487
Mapping a larger sample at higher resolution with coming surveys would show if the relation

00:02:55.487 --> 00:03:00.507
is truly universal, or shifts with cosmic time, and with how dense the surroundings are.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:06.980
Connecting Ridge near Shackleton Crater is one site where a crater wall was tested as reactor shielding

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:13.700
for a lunar habitat. Researchers simulated placing a 40 kilowatt nuclear reactor 1.5 meters above

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:19.460
the lunar surface on a rover. Radiation fell to roughly one-tenth of a ring per year behind a

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:25.760
crater three meters deep or a dirt hill three meters high. A crater wall 120 meters high there

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:31.740
brought habitat exposure down to four hundredths of a ring per year. Monte Carlo and particle software

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:37.354
tracked millions of particles leaving the core. Hubble observed the Milky Way's galactic bulge

00:03:37.354 --> 00:03:42.574
in red and near infrared light that matches the band the Nancy Grace Roman space telescope will use.

00:03:42.574 --> 00:03:47.754
Micro-lensing is a brief brightening caused when one star's gravity magnifies another,

00:03:48.174 --> 00:03:51.134
and Roman will use those events to find exoplanets.

00:03:51.514 --> 00:03:55.694
Those measurements will characterize stars before they cause those micro-lensing events.

00:03:56.254 --> 00:04:01.394
At high resolution, Hubble records how bright those individual stars are, plus their ages,

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:04.094
composition, and motion in a crowded field.

00:04:04.514 --> 00:04:10.534
They extend earlier treasury work, including the WFC3 Galactic Bulge Treasury Program, and

00:04:10.534 --> 00:04:16.321
the Sagittarius window eclipsing extra solar planet search. NASA researchers grew strawberries

00:04:16.321 --> 00:04:20.981
under flight-like chamber conditions and found delizzes beat a wild type that sent out too

00:04:20.981 --> 00:04:26.281
many runners. Cucumbers kept a steady yield of edible fruit in simulated space flight conditions,

00:04:26.841 --> 00:04:32.861
even as some leaves enlarged. Lemon basil cleared seed sanitization and early growth tests and now

00:04:32.861 --> 00:04:38.521
goes to plant pillow evaluation. On long-duration missions, these crops take up carbon dioxide,

00:04:38.521 --> 00:04:40.901
side, make oxygen and recycle water.

00:04:41.756 --> 00:04:47.396
Resolution Island appears in a NASA Landsat 9 operational land imager view of Fjordland's

00:04:47.396 --> 00:04:48.496
glacier-carved valleys.

00:04:49.096 --> 00:04:55.696
The island rises to Mount Clerc at 1069 meters, and the image is dated December 12, 2025.

00:04:56.496 --> 00:05:02.436
Thomas Henry Potts in 1872 put the island forward as a refuge for Kiwi and Kakapo.

00:05:02.436 --> 00:05:09.336
After the reserve was designated in 1891, caretaker Richard Henry moved more than 700 birds

00:05:09.336 --> 00:05:14.436
by rowboat. Stote control continues under a Department of Conservation program started

00:05:14.436 --> 00:05:20.701
in 2008, on an island that sits within swimming distance of the mainland. Boeing and Grace

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:27.061
Aerospace signed a NASA Mentor Prodigé Agreement valued at nearly $500,000 on October 29,

00:05:27.061 --> 00:05:33.661
29th, 2026 at the US Space and Rocket Center in Huntsville. NASA is simplifying applications

00:05:33.661 --> 00:05:38.501
to the Small Business Supplier Development Program and cutting administrative requirements.

00:05:39.141 --> 00:05:43.421
The pairing is meant to grow Grace's work on mission-critical aerospace hardware and

00:05:43.421 --> 00:05:49.109
to strengthen the domestic industrial base. Public Telescope Archives, Tech Times reported,

00:05:49.689 --> 00:05:55.349
yielded dozens of transit-like signals around nearby stars after open AI codecs and astramoddles

00:05:55.349 --> 00:05:58.449
scanned them, and those signals remain unconfirmed.

00:05:58.909 --> 00:06:01.769
A search for extraterrestrial intelligence or SETI,

00:06:02.249 --> 00:06:04.029
astronomer checked two of those signals

00:06:04.029 --> 00:06:06.149
against existing radio data and found

00:06:06.149 --> 00:06:08.349
no confirmed extraterrestrial origin.

